From 2b6f64160e1071b71a8541d7b9cad213ae99c2f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:19:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/97] diagnostics: steady_ns on [rate-census]; WAIT_REG_MEM
 poll-iteration census

[rate-census] lines carry steady_ns (steady_clock) so profiler samples can be
mapped to census seconds without the verbose-only frame-time lines.
WAIT_REG_MEM census (from the cycle-202 Director scouting session): per wait,
poll iterations and sleep payload are accumulated locally and recorded once
when the wait matches (no per-iteration census work); per-second stats of
iterations, payload and duration per poll target. Census-gated; no change
when WWE13_RATE_CENSUS is unset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/rex/diagnostics/rate_census.h |   7 +-
 src/core/rate_census.cpp              | 105 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/graphics/command_processor.cpp    |  33 +++++---
 3 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/rex/diagnostics/rate_census.h b/include/rex/diagnostics/rate_census.h
index ffde2f5..250f2eb 100644
--- a/include/rex/diagnostics/rate_census.h
+++ b/include/rex/diagnostics/rate_census.h
@@ -71,8 +71,11 @@ uint64_t NowNs();
